# Gateway config — hardened 2026-10-23 (Task 16 / finding 16e-002).
#
# The previous wildcard rule (`query XTransformPort=*` → reverse_proxy
# localhost:{query.XTransformPort}) was a live OPEN PROXY to every localhost
# service (audit-proven: keeper :3040 and mtq-feed :3003 were reachable
# through :81). Both mini-services are now RETIRED locally (see
# mini-services/RETIREMENT-NOTE.md), so no transform port is needed at all.
#
# If a future mini-service legitimately needs gateway exposure, re-add the
# rule with the port PINNED — never a wildcard:
#
#   @transform_port_query {
#           query XTransformPort=3003
#   }
#   handle @transform_port_query {
#           reverse_proxy localhost:3003 { ... }
#   }
#
# NOTE: the RUNNING sandbox caddy uses /app/Caddyfile (root-owned, not
# editable from this session). This file is the repository template — apply
# the same change to /app/Caddyfile + `caddy reload` when platform access
# is available. Residual risk until then: the wildcard remains live in the
# running gateway but now proxies to dead ports (connection refused) for
# everything except :3000, which is the app itself.

:81 {
        handle {
                reverse_proxy localhost:3000 {
                        header_up Host {host}
                        header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}
                        header_up X-Forwarded-Proto {scheme}
                        header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
                }
        }
}
